    {
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "\"Without a fair price, logically, it would not be possible to fairly pay workers. (…) Joining ASOGUABO gave us many opportunities to move ahead, including a fair price. In addition, with the Fairtrade Premium we can improve the infrastructure in our plantation and benefit our staff. Thanks to ASOGUABO and Fairtrade we have a family.\""
    },
    {
      "tag": "h2",
      "text": "More than a label"
    },
    {
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Farmers, join us."
    }
  ],
  "body": [
    "Producers are at the heart of Fairtrade. Investing in a Fairtrade certification can give your producer organisation greater economic stability and help you to become more sustainable.",
    "Volatile global market prices, power imbalances in supply chains and the consequences of climate change are tough challenges for farmers and workers in Latin America, the Caribbean, Africa, the Middle East, Asia, and the Pacific region.",
    "Often too many trade risks and responsibilities are pushed onto these producers, making it difficult to achieve a price that pays for production and the labour going into it. New rules about respecting human rights within supply chains (HRDD) are coming into effect in several regions of the world.",
    "Without fairer trade agreements, producers are most likely left to pay the price for such important ethical regulations. Meanwhile crops are threatened by rising temperatures, floods and other effects of the changing climate, again increasing the pressure on producers.",
    "Under such challenging circumstances, Fairtrade aims to strengthen producers and help them to build resilience.",
    "+1.9k Producer organisations working with Fairtrade worldwide.",
    "With nearly two million farmers and workers part of the Fairtrade system, there are at least that many stories of how they and their communities are building sustainable livelihoods and a fairer future.",
    "Less volatile prices Less volatile prices There is a Fairtrade Minimum Price for most certifiable products. It provides producers with a safety net against falling market prices for their sold produce and allows for long-term planning.",
    "Additional Premium Additional Premium With the Fairtrade Premium, producers can improve the quality of their lives, communities, and businesses. It is an additional amount of money paid on top of the agreed Fairtrade price for sold certified goods, which producers decide democratically how to use. The Fairtrade Premium is often invested in education, healthcare, and farm improvements to increase income.",
    "Have your say Have your say Fairtrade certified farmers and workers co-own and manage Fairtrade International – through elected delegates participating in the board of directors, key committees, and consultation processes, producers can influence Fairtrade’s strategy, standards, prices and premiums.",
    "Strong organisations Strong organisations With Fairtrade, small-scale farmer groups have a democratic structure and transparent administration. In plantations and hired labour settings, workers form a committee that decides on the use of the Fairtrade Premium. Fairtrade offers support to achieve this and strengthens producer organisations in the process.",
    "Market opportunities Market opportunities Fairtrade is the most recognised ethical label in the world. Fairtrade’s global network of marketing organisations can extend producers' reach to connect with businesses seeking sustainably sourced products under a label they trust.",
    "Power of community Power of community Producer organizations can join one of the three regional Fairtrade Producer Networks which provide support, training and representation for producers in the global Fairtrade system. They represent small-scale producers, workers, and other producer stakeholders. Please visit their websites for further information.",
    "Jessica Ramón Sanmartín, banana farmer and member of Asociación de Pequeños Productores Bananeros ‘El Guabo’ (ASOGUABO) in Ecuador",
    "Are you a producer organization ready to unlock the door to incredible possibilities for your organization with Fairtrade? Explore the simple steps to actively engage with Fairtrade, creating a positive impact.",
    "Contact the Fairtrade Producer Network pertinent to your region to get started."
  ],
